# Lesson 7-5 — Systems of Inequalities

Source: Module 7, Lesson 7-5, `Int1_0705_practice.docx`.

## Today's Goals

* Graph systems of linear inequalities and identify the common solution region.
* Write systems that represent graphs and context constraints.
* Test a point against every inequality in a system.

## Learn: Systems of Inequalities

A solution must satisfy every inequality. Graph each boundary on the same coordinate plane. Use a dashed boundary for a strict inequality. Use a solid boundary when equality is included. Select the correct side of each boundary. The common region is the solution set. Check the variable domain when you interpret a context solution.

